	affiliations = {Ltd., Zhangzhou, China; Chinese Academy of Agricultural Sciences, Feed Research Institute, Beijing, China},
	abstract = {This experiment was conducted to investigate the effects of fermented soft pellet feed on growth performance, serum indices, hepatopancreas and intestine morphology and intestinal flora of Litopenaeus vannamei. Three hundred healthy Litopenaeus vannamei with the same specifications of (3.35±0.08) g were randomly divided into 2 groups with 3 replicates per group and 50 shrimp per replicate. The control group was fed the basal diet, and the experimental group was fed the experimental diet in which 5% of the basal diet was replaced by fermented soft pellet feed. Fermented soft pellet feed was prepared by fermentation using Lactobacillus rhamnosus, Bacillus subtilis, Saccharomyces cerevisiae and Cetobacterium somerae as mixed fermentation agent and pellet feed as fermentation substrate. The trial lasted for 6 weeks. The results showed as follows: 1) compared with the control group, the weight gain rate, specific growth rate and survival rate of Litopenaeus vannamei in experimental group were significantly increased (P<0.05), and the feed coefficient was significantly decreased (P<0.05). 2) Compared with the control group, the activity of acid phosphatase and lysozyme in serum of Litopenaeus vannamei in experimental group was significantly increased (P<0.05), and the malondialdehyde content in serum was significantly decreased (P<0.05). 3) Hepatopancreas section observation showed that the hepatopancreas of Litopenaeus vannamei in experimental group was closely arranged, the basement membrane between the hepatopancreas was intact, and the number of B and R cells was abundant; however, in the control group, the hepatopancreas was arranged loosely, the basement membrane was shed, B cells were damaged, and the number of R and E cells was reduced. The observation of midgut section showed that the villi on the free surface of intestinal epithelial cells in experimental group were arranged more neatly and closely, and the villus height was significantly higher than that in the control group. 4) The results of principal coordinate analysis (PCoA) and non-metric multidimensional scale (NMDS) analysis showed that the intestinal flora of Litopenaeus vannamei in experimental group was significantly different from that in the control group (P<0.05). The bacterial community composition analysis showed that compared with the control group, the relative abundances of intestinal unclassified_f_Rhodobacteraceae and Ruegeria in experimental group were increased, and the relative abundance of intestinal unclassified_f_Flavobacteriaceae was decreased. In conclusion, the fermented soft pellet feed can improve growth performance, enhance immunity, regulate intestinal flora and maintain hepatopancreas and intestine health of Litopenaeus vannamei. © 2023 Chinese Journal of Animal Science and Veterinary Medicine Co., Ltd.. All rights reserved.},
